</tier><tier id="TIE18" speaker="SPK0" category="en" type="a" display-name="FP [en]"><event start="T0" end="T1">Mr Pofalla, do you know how much a litre of diesel costs at the moment? </event>
<event start="T3" end="T5">How much ? </event>
<event start="T8" end="T10">One thirty-three is it . </event>
<event start="T10" end="T11">That's the national average </event>
<event start="T11" end="T12">You might have a cheap petrol station in Berlin . </event>
<event start="T12" end="T14">What does that do to your budget? </event>
<event start="T17" end="T19">How, I would rather like to ask Mrs Kastenhuber this. </event>
<event start="T19" end="T22">How does the diesel price increase affect you? </event>
<event start="T29" end="T31">There is no more in it . </event>
<event start="T33" end="T38">Ḿhm̀ ˙ I'll save the compliments now, which you could also do. </event>
<event start="T38" end="T39">Let's just leave it at that . </event>
<event start="T39" end="T42">Umm </event>
<event start="T42" end="T43">Mrs Bartel the diesel price for Kastenhubers is the energy costs for electricity and heating for you . </event>
<event start="T43" end="T48">And these have risen by sixty-five per cent in recent years . </event>
<event start="T48" end="T50">How have these increased heating and electricity costs changed your life? </event>
<event start="T61" end="T64">How do you do that? </event>
<event start="T75" end="T77">Ḿhm̀ </event>
<event start="T77" end="T81">That's not a quirk, but er ...</event>
<event start="T82" end="T84">Because you don't get along otherwise? </event>
<event start="T85" end="T87">Ḿhm̀ ˙</event>
<event start="T91" end="T92">Euro . </event>
<event start="T99" end="T103">Let's take another look at exactly what your finances look like . </event>
<event start="T103" end="T106">Mr Pofalla, a former bookseller and a working mother of three children from a dual-income household reported . </event>
<event start="T106" end="T107">How would you now answer the question " How is the middle class in Germany " ? </event>
