<event start="T522" end="T523">das hat sich ge</event>
<event start="T523" end="T524">ändert. </event>
<event start="T525" end="T526">((lacht kurz))˙ </event>
</tier><tier id="TIE23" speaker="SPK5" category="en" type="a" display-name="HB [en]"><event start="T195" end="T198">Yes, you'll have to explain it to me. </event>
<event start="T198" end="T199">You also made most of the programmes on marginal topics. </event>
<event start="T199" end="T211">You made a lot of programmes about managers' salaries, you talked a lot about Hartz Four minimum wages, but the concerns of the middle class, of those who go to work in the morning, who earn what is subsequently distributed by the state, because they pay the social security contributions, who pay the taxes, who actually pull the cart in Germany, these concerns were discussed far too little. </event>
<event start="T211" end="T225">And when Mr Pofalla says that the middle class has been relieved and the only thing he mentions is the unemployment insurance contribution, then you are neglecting the fact that this black-red coalition has gone one better with the biggest tax increase that we have had in the history of the Federal Republic with an increase in VAT, insurance tax and many other cuts, home ownership allowance, commuter allowance and much more, and of course this has particularly affected the middle class. </event>
<event start="T225" end="T229">The state is the main beneficiary of the current upturn. </event>
<event start="T229" end="T231">The big revenues - you can smile Mr Pofalla - the big revenues have come from the state. </event>
<event start="T231" end="T233">You said "lived beyond your means". </event>
<event start="T233" end="T234">Now you are taking it back from the citizens. </event>
<event start="T234" end="T237">There is not much left over for the citizens . </event>
<event start="T492" end="T498">Well, it's an investment for the health of the child / son, so I think it's good that no money is being saved on it, because that would be at the expense of the son's health. </event>
<event start="T498" end="T504">I find it hard that a hundred and thirty year old piano - if I've understood correctly - has to be used for this. </event>
<event start="T504" end="T505">I'm now ... </event>
<event start="T505" end="T506">I don't know exactly how expensive the braces are. </event>
<event start="T506" end="T510">You could have thought about whether you could have taken out a supplementary insurance policy early on with favourable premiums, for example, or a savings contract or other things. </event>
<event start="T510" end="T514">I know it's hard to have the leeway to do that but ...</event>
<event start="T521" end="T524">Yes, that has changed. </event>
<event start="T525" end="T526">˙</event>
</tier><tier id="TIE11" speaker="SPK5" category="akz" type="a" display-name=""><event start="T235" end="T236">—</event>
</tier><tier id="TIE17" speaker="SPK5" category="k" type="a" display-name="HB [k]"><event start="T206" end="T207">für: vom </event>
</tier><tier id="TIE12" category="nn" type="d" display-name="[nn]"><event start="T237" end="T239">((Publikum applaudiert, 9,4s)) </event>
<event start="T246" end="T247">((Jemand sagt "Aber die…")) </event>
<event start="T254" end="T255">((Husten)) </event>
<event start="T477" end="T483">((Publikum applaudiert, 7,6s)) </event>
<event start="T487" end="T488">• • • </event>
<event start="T488" end="T489">((Film wird eingespielt, 2min 9s)) </event>
<event start="T527" end="T528">((Aufnahme bricht ab)) </event>
</tier></basic-body>
